  "description": "The \u0027connections_with_failures\u0027 dataset provides detailed information about various connection attempts that have failed, including metadata and error messages. This dataset is particularly useful for diagnosing and troubleshooting connection issues in systems that rely on external services or APIs. Each entry in the dataset includes the name and type of the connection, the credentials mode, and the status of the connection test, which indicates whether the connection attempt was successful or failed. In cases of failure, the dataset provides a detailed error message that can help identify the cause of the issue, such as insufficient quota or incorrect credentials. Additional metadata includes information about who can use the connection, authentication parameters, and the last user to modify the connection settings. This dataset is valuable for system administrators and developers who need to ensure reliable connectivity and quickly resolve any issues that arise. By analyzing the patterns and common causes of failures, organizations can improve their connection configurations and reduce downtime.",
  "shortDesc": "Dataset of connection failures with error messages and metadata.",
